> OK Wizard who started with Ring of Regen and Wand of Fire finds a Bag of 
> Holding on level 2.  Down to level 5 and I find an altar.  Do some stuff 
> with saccing and such.  Last sac got me a four leaf clover.  I was 
> surrounded by killer bees and had 6 out of 37 hit points left.  Last great 
> act was to pray figuring that I would be healed.  So what happens?  Golden 
> glow.  Nothing else.  Of course I died from one of the bees as I could not 
> kill them both in one turn because they were not lined up and I was in a 
> corner on the altar. 

AFAIK it works like this in vanilla, and also in Slash'EM:
If your current HP < or = 1/7 of your max HP rounded down OR if your 
current HP is less than six it is considered a major problem.

With 6/37 HP you would not meet any of these requirements, and hence it 
was not considered a trouble (major or otherwise).

What happened when you prayed was that you got the most favorable result 
possible, a "fix all major and minor problems, and also grant a favor" 
jackpot. Perhaps it fixed some major/minor problems for you, cured your 
hunger or something, and then decided randomly with luck influence that 
you should also receive the golden glow favor (+5 max HP and some other 
things).

A 37 HP character should take much effort to stay out of the situation 
you describe, since relying on getting a chance to pray in the 1-5 HP 
interval is a very dangerous practice when cornered by killer bees. 
Perhaps steppping off the altar and engraving something in the ground 
would have done you better.

> Now this has happened many times to me and I finally got so fed up with it.  

I guess that you must have based your idea that praying will help heal 
your current HP on experience. That *is* the fun part of 
Nethack/Slash'EM really, finding out such things by playing and then 
being able to use them, right? And the same goes for the new knowledge 
you have now acquired, right? So you could feel that nice feeling of 
'now I have learnt even more and am even better at this game' rather 
than the 'I am fed up with not always getting a current HP boost when I 
pray and am not at max HP'. 

